    "items": [
      {
        "type": "heading1",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "Lessons from Israel’s Past"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "label",
        "verse_numbers": [],
        "lines": [
          "A Maskil of Asaph."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          1
        ],
        "lines": [
          "My people, hear my instruction;",
          "listen to the words from my mouth."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          2
        ],
        "lines": [
          "I will declare wise sayings;",
          "I will speak mysteries from the past —"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          3
        ],
        "lines": [
          "things we have heard and known",
          "and that our ancestors have passed down to us."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          4
        ],
        "lines": [
          "We will not hide them from their children,",
          "but will tell a future generation",
          "the praiseworthy acts of the Lord,",
          "his might, and the wondrous works",
          "he has performed."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          5
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He established a testimony in Jacob",
          "and set up a law in Israel,",
          "which he commanded our ancestors",
          "to teach to their children"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          6
        ],
        "lines": [
          "so that a future generation —",
          "children yet to be born #— #might know.",
          "They were to rise and tell their children"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          7
        ],
        "lines": [
          "so that they might put their confidence in God",
          "and not forget God’s works,",
          "but keep his commands."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          8
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Then they would not be like their ancestors,",
          "a stubborn and rebellious generation,",
          "a generation whose heart was not loyal",
          "and whose spirit was not faithful to God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          9
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Ephraimite archers turned back",
          "on the day of battle."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          10
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They did not keep God’s covenant",
          "and refused to live by his law."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          11
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They forgot what he had done,",
          "the wondrous works he had shown them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          12
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He worked wonders in the sight of their ancestors",
          "in the land of Egypt, the territory of Zoan."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          13
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He split the sea and brought them across;",
          "the water stood firm like a wall."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          14
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He led them with a cloud by day",
          "and with a fiery light throughout the night."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          15
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He split rocks in the wilderness",
          "and gave them drink as abundant as the depths."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          16
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He brought streams out of the stone",
          "and made water flow down like rivers."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          17
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But they continued to sin against him,",
          "rebelling in the desert against the Most High."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          18
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They deliberately tested God,",
          "demanding the food they craved."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          19
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They spoke against God, saying,",
          "“Is God able to provide food in the wilderness?"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          20
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Look! He struck the rock and water gushed out;",
          "torrents overflowed.",
          "But can he also provide bread",
          "or furnish meat for his people? ”"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          21
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Therefore, the Lord heard and became furious;",
          "then fire broke out against Jacob,",
          "and anger flared up against Israel"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          22
        ],
        "lines": [
          "because they did not believe God",
          "or rely on his salvation."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          23
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He gave a command to the clouds above",
          "and opened the doors of heaven."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          24
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He rained manna for them to eat;",
          "he gave them grain from heaven."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          25
        ],
        "lines": [
          "People ate the bread of angels.",
          "He sent them an abundant supply of food."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          26
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He made the east wind blow in the skies",
          "and drove the south wind by his might."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          27
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He rained meat on them like dust,",
          "and winged birds like the sand of the seas."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          28
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He made them fall in the camp,",
          "all around the tents."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          29
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The people ate and were completely satisfied,",
          "for he gave them what they craved."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          30
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Before they had turned from what they craved,",
          "while the food was still in their mouths,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          31
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God’s anger flared up against them,",
          "and he killed some of their best men.",
          "He struck down Israel’s fit young men."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          32
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Despite all this, they kept sinning",
          "and did not believe his wondrous works."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          33
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He made their days end in futility,",
          "their years in sudden disaster."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          34
        ],
        "lines": [
          "When he killed some of them,",
          "the rest began to seek him;",
          "they repented and searched for God."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          35
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They remembered that God was their rock,",
          "the Most High God, their Redeemer."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          36
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But they deceived him with their mouths,",
          "they lied to him with their tongues,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          37
        ],
        "lines": [
          "their hearts were insincere toward him,",
          "and they were unfaithful to his covenant."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          38
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Yet he was compassionate;",
          "he atoned for their iniquity",
          "and did not destroy them.",
          "He often turned his anger aside",
          "and did not unleash all his wrath."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          39
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He remembered that they were only flesh,",
          "a wind that passes and does not return."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          40
        ],
        "lines": [
          "How often they rebelled against him",
          "in the wilderness",
          "and grieved him in the desert."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          41
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They constantly tested God",
          "and provoked the Holy One of Israel."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          42
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They did not remember his power shown",
          "on the day he redeemed them from the foe,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          43
        ],
        "lines": [
          "when he performed his miraculous signs in Egypt",
          "and his wonders in the territory of Zoan."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          44
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He turned their rivers into blood,",
          "and they could not drink from their streams."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          45
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He sent among them swarms of flies,",
          "which fed on them,",
          "and frogs, which devastated them."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          46
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He gave their crops to the caterpillar",
          "and the fruit of their labor to the locust."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          47
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He killed their vines with hail",
          "and their sycamore fig trees with a flood."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          48
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He handed over their livestock to hail",
          "and their cattle to lightning bolts."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          49
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He sent his burning anger against them:",
          "fury, indignation, and calamity —",
          "a band of deadly messengers. ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          50
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He cleared a path for his anger.",
          "He did not spare them from death",
          "but delivered their lives to the plague."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          51
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He struck all the firstborn in Egypt,",
          "the first progeny of the tents of Ham."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          52
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He led his people out like sheep",
          "and guided them like a flock in the wilderness."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          53
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He led them safely, and they were not afraid;",
          "but the sea covered their enemies."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          54
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He brought them to his holy territory,",
          "to the mountain his right hand acquired."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          55
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He drove out nations before them.",
          "He apportioned their inheritance by lot",
          "and settled the tribes of Israel in their tents."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          56
        ],
        "lines": [
          "But they rebelliously tested the Most High God,",
          "for they did not keep his decrees."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          57
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They treacherously turned away like their ancestors;",
          "they became warped like a faulty bow."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          58
        ],
        "lines": [
          "They enraged him with their high places",
          "and provoked his jealousy with their carved images."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          59
        ],
        "lines": [
          "God heard and became furious;",
          "he completely rejected Israel."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          60
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He abandoned the tabernacle at Shiloh,",
          "the tent where he resided among mankind."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          61
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He gave up his strength to captivity",
          "and his splendor to the hand of a foe."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          62
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He surrendered his people to the sword",
          "because he was enraged with his heritage."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          63
        ],
        "lines": [
          "Fire consumed his chosen young men,",
          "and his young women had no wedding songs. ,"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          64
        ],
        "lines": [
          "His priests fell by the sword,",
          "and the widows could not lament."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          65
        ],
        "lines": [
          "The Lord awoke as if from sleep,",
          "like a warrior from the effects of wine."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          66
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He beat back his foes;",
          "he gave them lasting disgrace."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          67
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He rejected the tent of Joseph",
          "and did not choose the tribe of Ephraim."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          68
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He chose instead the tribe of Judah,",
          "Mount Zion, which he loved."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          69
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He built his sanctuary like the heights,",
          "like the earth that he established forever."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          70
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He chose David his servant",
          "and took him from the sheep pens;"
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          71
        ],
        "lines": [
          "he brought him from tending ewes",
          "to be shepherd over his people Jacob —",
          "over Israel, his inheritance."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "verse_numbers": [
          72
        ],
        "lines": [
          "He shepherded them with a pure heart",
          "and guided them with his skillful hands."
        ],
        "rlw_lines": []
      }
    ]
  },
